---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Thierry Heumann — builder of small, focused web apps.">
  <article class="pt-10 pb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">About</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        I'm Thierry Heumann. THeApps is where the things I build end up — the
        name reads two ways, "The Apps" and "TH e-apps," which is either clever
        or a pun I've talked myself into.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most of what I make comes from the same place: a group of people trying
        to coordinate something, and a group chat that isn't up to the job.
        Chat is great for banter and terrible for state. Who's actually coming?
        Who paid? Is there room for one more? The answer is somewhere in a
        thread nobody wants to scroll.
      </p>

      <p>
        So the apps tend to be small and pointed. They do the handful of things
        chat does badly, and stay out of the way for everything else.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
